-- title:
--   Ordinary condition descends along an injective local map
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ and $B$ be commutative local rings, let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring with algebra structures on $A$ and $B$, and let $\varphi : A \to B$ be an injective ring homomorphism that is local (it carries non-units to non-units). Let $\rho$ be a [`GaloisRepAdic`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16) over $A$: a finite free $A$-module $V$ with $\operatorname{rank}_A V = 2$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ (realised as the $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphisms of $\operatorname{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$) to $\operatorname{End}_A V$ which is adically continuous, i.e. for every $n$ there is a finite extension $L/\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that every $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise satisfies $\rho(\sigma)v - v \in \mathfrak{m}_A^n V$ for all $v$. Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$, let $S$ be a finite set of naturals, and assume the image of $p$ in $B$ is nilpotent. Assume that the base change $\rho \otimes_A B$ along $\varphi$, with $\sigma$ acting by $\rho(\sigma) \otimes \mathrm{id}$, satisfies [`GaloisRep.ordinaryCondition 𝒪 p S`](def/GaloisRep_LocalConditions.html#L28), that is: (i) $p \in \mathfrak{m}_B$ and for all $n$, all $\sigma$ and all $a \in \mathbb{N}$ with $\sigma\mu = \mu^a$ for every $p^n$-th root of unity $\mu$, one has $\det \rho(\sigma) \equiv a$ modulo the ideal generated by $p^n$; (ii) for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $p$ there is a submodule spanned by the first vector of some basis which is stable under the decomposition group of $P$ and on which the quotient action of the inertia subgroup of $P$ is trivial, in the sense that $\rho(\sigma)v - v$ lies in it for all $v$; (iii) $\rho$ is unramified at every prime $q \notin S$, i.e. $\rho(\sigma) = 1$ for every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of any valuation subring lying over $q$. The conclusion is that $\rho$ itself satisfies [`GaloisRep.ordinaryCondition 𝒪 p S`](def/GaloisRep_LocalConditions.html#L28) over $A$. The definition of `ordinaryCondition` makes no reference to the $\mathcal{O}$-algebra structures, which only occur in its binders.
--
--   This is the sub-object axiom for the ordinary local deformation condition in Mazur's axiomatic framework: the ordinary condition at $p$, together with the cyclotomic determinant and unramifiedness outside $S$, is reflected by an injective local base change. It is used in assembling [`GaloisRep.isDeformationCondition_ordinaryCondition`](thm.html#GaloisRep.isDeformationCondition_ordinaryCondition) and in the corresponding statement for the strict ordinary condition.
